## 5. Pre-Flight Distribution Verification Checklist

Before triggering a production build or opening a store deployment request, verify the following:

* **[ ] Application Bundle ID Convention:** Android and iOS application identifiers must strictly adhere to `com.enterprise.<appname>`.
* **[ ] TGRC Governance Submission:** Form submitted on the internal portal with the complete Excel manifest detailing target release channels, data classification, and authentication endpoints.
* **[ ] Test Account Credentials:** Active, valid demo login credentials (username and password) provided in the release notes for store review team evaluation without requiring SMS/biometric two-factor hardware.
* **[ ] Play Store Visual Assets:** High-resolution 512x512 PNG app icon and 1024x500 JPEG/PNG feature graphic prepared with zero alpha transparency.
* **[ ] App Store Multi-Device Screenshots:** Minimum of 4 screenshots uploaded for each required device form factor (iPhone 6.7" Display, iPhone 6.5" Display, iPad Pro 12.9").
* **[ ] Privacy Policy URL:** Live, publicly accessible corporate privacy policy link active on HTTPS.
* **[ ] Entitlements & Identity Setup:** For internal enterprise business apps, identity groups and entitlement owners configured in `access.enterprise.internal`.
* **[ ] Code Signing Vault Verification:** Android Release Keystore (`.jks`) and Apple Distribution Certificate (`.p12`) confirmed valid with at least 60 days remaining before expiration.




