## 5. TGRC Pre-Deployment Security Sign-Off

Deploying any mobile application to the **Enterprise UAT** or **Enterprise PROD** app stores strictly requires prior authorization from the **Technology Governance &amp; Regulatory Compliance (TGRC)** board:

1. **Submit TGRC Request Form:** The development team submits the mobile deployment request form available on the internal developer service portal (`https://myid.enterprise.internal/mobile-deploy`).
2. **Attach Complete Excel Manifest:** The request must include the official enterprise deployment manifest spreadsheet containing:
   * Target Application ID (`com.enterprise.<appname>`).
   * Production API backend hostnames and data classification level (Confidential, Restricted).
   * User authentication mechanism (Okta SSO, OAuth 2.0 PKCE).
   * Datadog RUM client tokens and PII sanitization proof.
3. **Turnaround SLA:** TGRC typically reviews and approves submissions within **24 to 48 hours**. Emergency security hotfixes can request expedited approval via the on-call TGRC duty lead.





