## 1. Mandatory Release Assets & Information

To publish an Android mobile application to the public Google Play Store, the development team must prepare and submit a strictly governed set of metadata, cryptographic assets, and store listing collateral:

* **Signed Android App Bundle (`.aab`):** The release binary compiled with production optimizations, R8 shrinking, and signed with the enterprise upload key or unified release certificate.
* **App Name ("Visible in Play Store"):** The official public brand title displayed on Google Play.
* **App Search Keywords:** Relevant discovery keywords used by prospective commercial clients and customers to locate the application on mobile devices.
* **App Category:** Primary category declaration (strictly **Business** or **Utility** for enterprise applications).
* **Test Account Credentials:** Active username and password provided in the Play Console *App Access* section so Google review engineers can authenticate.
* **Privacy Policy URL:** Publicly reachable HTTPS link to the corporate privacy statement.

