## 2. Field Description Character Limit Notes

Google Play strictly enforces character length boundaries on all store listing copy. Submissions exceeding these limits are immediately rejected by the Play Console validation engine:

<div class="portal-table-wrap">
  <table class="portal-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Store Listing Field</th>
        <th>Character Limit</th>
        <th>Display Behavior &amp; User Experience</th>
        <th>Optimization Best Practice</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>App Title</strong></td>
        <td><strong>50 characters</strong><br/>(30 recommended)</td>
        <td>The primary title displayed in search rankings, category charts, and the app listing hero banner. One localized title allowed per supported language.</td>
        <td>Keep concise: <code>[Brand Name] - [Core Function]</code>. Do not include promotional terms like "Free", "Best", or "#1".</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Short Description</strong></td>
        <td><strong>80 characters</strong></td>
        <td>The very first copy users see when viewing the app's detail page on the mobile Play Store app. Users expand this text to view the full description.</td>
        <td>Focus on the primary value proposition: <em>"Manage grain contracts, track real-time commodity bids, and scale your harvest."</em></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Full Description</strong></td>
        <td><strong>4,000 characters</strong></td>
        <td>Detailed overview of the app's features, capabilities, workflows, customer support channels, and security credentials.</td>
        <td>Structure with bullet points, feature headings, and operational prerequisites. Avoid keyword stuffing.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

