## 4. Reviewer Test Credentials & App Access Configuration

Google Play Review Guideline 2.1 mandates that reviewers must be able to authenticate and inspect all primary app workflows. If the application requires a login, the release team must provide valid credentials:

```text
Google Play Console -> App Content -> App Access -> "All or some functionality is restricted"
-> Add Credentials:
   - Account Name: "Enterprise Automated Reviewer"
   - Username: play-tester@enterprise.internal
   - Password: [Secure High-Entropy Password]
   - Additional Notes: "Test account configured with simulated demo orders. No hardware SMS 2FA required."
```

<div class="portal-alert-box info">
  <div class="portal-alert-title">TWO-FACTOR AUTHENTICATION (2FA) BYPASS RULE</div>
  <p>
    Google Play reviewers cannot receive hardware SMS codes or enterprise push authenticators (Okta Verify / Microsoft Authenticator). For store test accounts, engineering must either provide fixed universal OTP codes (e.g., <code>123456</code>) or exempt the review username from 2FA requirements in staging/production identity gateways.
  </p>
</div>

