## 3. Mandatory TGRC Pre-Deployment Security Approval

Under corporate compliance standards, **no application can be released to UAT or Production without prior approval from Technology Governance &amp; Regulatory Compliance (TGRC)**:

```text
Build Artifact (.aab / .ipa)
       │
       ▼
[Submit TGRC Request on Internal Portal] ──► Attach Completed Excel Manifest
       │
       ▼
[TGRC Review: Data Privacy, Auth Security, PII Masking]
       │
       ├──► APPROVED: Promoted to UAT or PROD
       └──► REJECTED: Remediation required (Security Findings)
```

### Pre-Deployment Manifest Requirements:
Development teams must download, populate, and attach the official **TGRC Mobile Deployment Manifest** (Excel file) containing:
1. **Application Identity:** Full app name, bundle ID, version number, and build code.
2. **Data Classification:** Confidential, Restricted, or Public data handling classification.
3. **API &amp; Backend Endpoints:** List of all production backend microservices and domain hostnames consumed by the client.
4. **Authentication &amp; Tokens:** User sign-in flows (Okta, Entra ID, OAuth 2.0 PKCE) and token storage mechanism.
5. **Observability Verification:** Datadog RUM configuration and confirmation that all PII masking filters are enabled.

