## 5. Automated Bitrise Code Signing Integration

To prevent unencrypted certificate leakage onto developer workstations, all signing keys are securely mounted into memory only during CI/CD build execution:

```yaml
# bitrise.yml
workflows:
  release-prod-ios:
    steps:
    - certificate-and-profile-installer@1:
        inputs:
        - default_certificate_passphrase: $BITRISEIO_CERTIFICATE_PASSPHRASE
    - xcode-archive@5:
        inputs:
        - export_method: app-store # or enterprise
        - distribution_type: app-store
        - compile_bitcode: "no"

  release-prod-android:
    steps:
    - sign-apk@1:
        inputs:
        - android_app: $BITRISE_AAB_PATH
        - keystore_url: $BITRISEIO_ANDROID_KEYSTORE_URL
        - keystore_password: $BITRISEIO_ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD
        - keystore_alias: $BITRISEIO_ANDROID_KEYSTORE_ALIAS
        - private_key_password: $BITRISEIO_ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD
```

